<title>ARGENTINA: Buenos Aires province to dock strikers' pay.</title>
<headline>Buenos Aires province to dock strikers' pay.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's biggest province Buenos Aires will dock the wages of public sector workers who join a 36-hour national strike Thursday, local government sources told the state news agency Telam.</p>
<p>The protest against federal fiscal and labor policies began at noon local time/1100 EDT and includes a demonstration outside the government house at 1500 local time/1400 EDT.</p>
<p>Buenos Aires is a traditionally Peronist-ruled province led by Governor Eduardo Duhalde, who hopes to succeed President Carlos Menem in 1999 general elections.</p>
<p>-- Carmen Pignotti, Buenos Aires Newsroom 541 318-0657</p>
